> any updates on ways to run logistic models in lavaan

Marginal ML is simply too computationally intensive to be feasible when written in R.  This will not be implemented in lavaan until the core can be replaced with a C++ engine.  If you have any funding available to facilitate prioritizing this process, please consider donating to lavaan:

https://lavaan.ugent.be/

Or contacting the developer about including such an endeavor in a grant application.  Applying for grants purely to develop lavaan has been unsuccessful in the past, but it might be more feasible to include it in an attractive research project that you can argue needs some software development to accomplish its analytical goals.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

