Hi Dr. Christian,
I apologize for the mistake in the code from my previous message. I was typing quickly and didn't notice that. The code was entered correctly in R, as shown below, and that produced the error message. As for the moderation, the "moderator.a := a2 - a1" aligns better with my objective because it reflects the path that is being moderated. Thanks for the suggestion.
The issue I'm facing is with the bootstrapping, which fails to run due to labeling (i.e., c(a1, a2), c(b1, b2)) needed to obtain the path coefficient for each group. When I remove the label or include only a single label (either a1/b1 or a2/b2), the code runs without errors; however, the result is the overall regression coefficient estimate instead of getting separate estimates for Group 1 and Group 2.
Is there any way to obtain the bootstrap estimates and confidence intervals for each group while also being able to estimate the moderated mediation index?

Thank you!

#Analysis code

modmediated_lv2 <- "

inter_latent =~ img1 + img2 + img3

totanxscore ~ c(a1,a2)*inter_latent

TRT_Ad  ~  inter_latent   + c(b1,b2)* totanxscore  + age

#Defining new parameters

a1b1 := a1 * b1        #Indirect effect for group 1 and group 2

a2b2 := a2 * b2

modmed := a2 - a1   # Moderated mediation index

"

MGSEM_boot _fit <- sem(modmediated_lv2, data_clean, group = "provt",

                             ordered = "TRT_Ad ",

                            se = "bootstrap", bootstrap = 5000, estimator = "DWLS",

                            group.equal = "loadings")

                             verbose = TRUE)

